review:
Best Resident Evil so far. Much better than classics and Village.
11/10

@Vizpies buy this game, it works with GamesForWindows

If i could find a sentence to describe this game, it would be: 'guilty pleasure';

Game is not cannon, it's basically a cover-based third person shoot-em-up;
In the main campaign you'll be controlling a squad of Umbrella Spec Ops in finding and destroying any data that could compromise Umbrella's image.

You'll be fighting your common zombies, crimson-heads, lickers, parasite-zombies, zombie-dogs, hunters, Nemesis, Mr Birkin and MR-X-like-tyrants. Aside from the B.O.Ws mentioned, you'll be fighting off government spec-ops forces most of the time. The campaign is not long and can be completed in maybe under 6 or so hours. You have a variety of guns to pick, from primary to secondary guns, being Assault Rifles, submachineguns, machineguns, bolt-action rifles, shotguns and then a small variety of pistols respectively;

Gameplay gets old fast as you fight off the same enemies again and again, increasing the difficulty means enemies become bullet sponges and you, fragile. 

The only DLC that's worth it is the Spec-Ops #1 and #2, as it adds a new campaign on the same size of the original but instead of fighting for Umbrella, ur fighting as the government spec-ops. The rest of the downloadable content comes in form of new and unneeded guns and a costume settings for the original campaign (which only just changes the character clothes colour)

Edit: Yeah i'm halfway through the DLC campaign and i gotta say that even tho it's cool to see some more iconic characters like Jill and Nemesis (again), it's like i'm doing the same things again and again, you have to go through some of the same locations you went in the main campaign to do the opposite of what you did in the previous (main campaign had you destroy any evidence in the Raccoon City Hall, in the DLC you have to go through the same rooms but this time you have to find evidence, it's as if it contradicts what we've already done in the base campaign)

Resident Evil: L4D2 

No cloud saves;
Need GFWL;
Online is dead;
You fight too many human soldiers in both campaign;
Some people can't even launch the game or it just crashes.

It's fun and decently active rn, not amazing but not terrible. get it on sale

/// update 3/24/2025 
Game is still unplayable, and is unlikely to ever come back. Given that it's been so long and Capcom can't even have new releases function properly on PC I have zero faith in this game ever working again

[b]Resident Evil: Operation Raccoon City[/b] is a action game based on the main Resident Evil universe, the events on this game are not to be considered canon, they are mostly a "what if" scenario showing how things could have been if Umbrela was better prepared to handle the events that happened during Resident Evil 2 and 3.
In this game you play as a Umbrela Elite Squad that is sent to the William Birkin's lab underneath Raccoon City to retrieve a sample of the G-Virus and to destroy any evidence that connects Umbrela to the virus outbreak that has killed thounsands of people and turned them into zombies.

[b]Pros:[/b]
• Good graphics for relatively old game;
• Interesting level system that gives you reason to replay the game;
• Interesting alternate story showing a bit more of Umbrela's actions;
• Extremely fun to play in co-op with up to 4 friends.

[b]Cons[/b]
• Games for Windows Live (and not a chance to port this to Steamworks anytime soon, the company that made this game for Capcom no longer exists, therefore it's not possible to port it without high costs and we all know Capcom won't bother);
• Amazingly dumb AI (and not only 1 of them, but 3);
• Expensive for a old game and seldom goes on sale.


All in all, RE:ORC is a great game. It's fun to play with your friends and it's nice to see other side of things around Raccoon City.
People like to call this "a great action game based in Resident Evil but a bad Resident Evil", but most people do not realize that this game isn't canon and the events here are not part of the original RE timeline, it's just a "what if" games showing Umbrela's side of the Raccoon City outbreak.
The Games for Windows Live is the main issue here, it's broken and particularly worse if you use Windows 8+. 


I do recommend this game, should it ever go on sale (which is hard to happen), try to get it for you and a couple of your friends, you'll have lots of coop gun together.

Très bonne idée de départ ce petit hors série, mais la jouabilitée n'est pas top. Le mécanisme est le même que sur RE4 ou RE5 et aurait gagné à être plus fluide .... Mais pouvoir jouer Hunk ou d'autres est très plaisant!
